# Lumina Edge — Project Context for Goose

You are operating within the Lumina Edge local LLM inference framework. Below are the critical platform rules, architecture details, and conventions you must follow.

## Platform Rules (Never Violate)

- **macOS (Darwin)**: MLX (mlx_lm) backend ONLY. Never use llama.cpp on macOS. Shell scripts (.sh). Apple Silicon M1-M4 required.
- **Linux**: llama.cpp + Vulkan backend. Shell scripts (.sh). GPU offloading via --n-gpu-layers. CUDA/NVIDIA also supported.
- **Windows**: llama.cpp backend. PowerShell scripts (.ps1). Vulkan or CUDA depending on GPU.

## Architecture Overview

Lumina Edge runs a local OpenAI-compatible API server on port 8090:
- macOS: MLX backend via `scripts/mlx_backend.py --mode api`
- Linux/Win: `bin/llama-server` listens on port 8090
- API endpoint: `http://localhost:8090/v1` (OpenAI-compatible chat/completions)
- Management endpoint: `http://localhost:8081/api/health`
- Config file: `config.json` at repo root (JSON format)

## Repository Structure

```
/
├── .goosehints              # This file — project context for Goose
├── config.json              # All runtime settings (model, port, ctx_size, etc.)
├── pipeline_api.py          # FastAPI server for multi-agent pipeline orchestrator
├── requirements.txt         # Python deps (Linux/Win)
├── scripts/
│   ├── requirements-macos.txt  # Python deps (macOS only)
│   ├── mlx_backend.py          # MLX inference server (macOS)
│   ├── mlx_optimize_system.py  # macOS memory optimizer
│   ├── system_optimizer.py     # Linux memory optimizer
│   ├── windows_prelaunch.ps1   # Windows memory optimizer
│   ├── model-router.py         # Multi-model parallel loader
│   ├── model-converter.py      # Format converter (safetensors → GGUF)
│   ├── ingest_docs.py         # RAG document ingestion
│   └── query_docs.py          # RAG document query
├── bin/                    # llama.cpp binaries (Linux/Win only)
├── models/                 # Model files (GGUF, MLX, safetensors)
├── start_api.sh / .ps1     # API-only launcher (one script per platform)
├── start_lumina.sh / .ps1  # Full stack launcher
├── start-goose.sh / .ps1   # Launch Lumina + Goose (this project)
├── install-goose.sh / .ps1 # Goose installer
├── ui/                     # Electron/React web UI
├── core/                   # Node.js API gateway
└── orchestrator/           # Python multi-agent pipeline
```

## Key Configuration (config.json)

- `api_port`: 8090 (the OpenAI-compatible endpoint)
- `model`: Model filename relative to models/
- `ctx_size`: Context window in tokens (default 16384)
- `n_gpu_layers`: GPU offloading layers (99 = all)
- `temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k`, `repeat_penalty`: Sampling params
- `gpu_type`: nvidia / intel / amd / apple_silicon

## Coding Conventions

- All scripts must be platform-aware: check `uname -s` for macOS vs Linux
- Windows uses PowerShell (.ps1) with `$IsWindows` detection
- macOS uses MLX (never llama.cpp); Linux/Win use llama.cpp
- Python scripts use `python3` shebang
- Config is read from config.json using python3 helper or PowerShell ConvertFrom-Json

## Goose-Specific Notes

- Goose connects to `http://localhost:8090/v1` as its LLM backend
- Provider: openai (via OPENAI_HOST=http://localhost:8090/v1)
- Model is auto-detected from GET /v1/models — never hardcode
- The developer builtin extension is enabled for shell + file system access
- API key can be any non-empty string (Lumina doesn't authenticate)
- Streaming is enabled
- All operations are local — no cloud, no external keys

## Available Start Commands

```bash
# Start Lumina Edge API only
./start_api.sh                    # macOS/Linux
.\start_api.ps1                   # Windows

# Start full Lumina stack (API + UI)
./start_lumina.sh                 # macOS/Linux
.\start_lumina.ps1                # Windows

# Start Lumina + Goose (this workflow)
./start-goose.sh                  # macOS/Linux
.\start-goose.ps1                 # Windows
```
